= How to Read This Document


This Program Manual is structured to serve four audiences simultaneously. Each audience has a different reason for opening the book and a different reading path that leads to what they need. Reading the entire volume end-to-end gives the most complete picture; the reading orders below are for readers who want the relevant content first.



== For Brand Legal Teams


You are reading this manual to evaluate whether HMTc is defensible enough to recommend that your client enter the program. You will be asked, by a CEO or general counsel, whether participation creates litigation exposure or reduces it. Your conclusion needs to survive a hostile reviewer at a competitor or a plaintiff's expert in a deposition.


*Recommended reading order:*

+ *Part 1* in full. The structural argument explains why the program exists; the financial argument quantifies what your client faces without it.
+ *Part 2.4 (The Confidential Remediation Track)*. The most important single chapter for legal defensibility. The track exists so that brands not yet at certification standards can enter, build a documented improvement record, and shift the legal narrative from "knew and did nothing" to "knew, enrolled, and has third-party-verified evidence of continuous improvement."
+ *Part 2.6 (Decision Rules under Measurement Uncertainty)* and *Part 2.7 (Data Governance and Integrity)*. These chapters describe the analytical and documentary discipline that makes the program's evidence record admissible.
+ *Part 5.2 (Program-Level Adversarial Read)*. The structured response to every category of attack you might face against the program. Read this chapter if your client is being asked to defend their participation against a hostile inquiry.
+ *The product chapter in Part 3* matching your client's category. This is the chapter that will be attached as an exhibit to their licensing agreement.



== For Retailer Compliance and QA Teams


You are reading this manual to decide whether to recognize HMTc as a basis for shelf access or assortment approval. You need to confirm that the program is rigorous enough to substitute for your own ingredient-level surveillance, and that participating brands meet a meaningfully higher bar than non-participating brands.


*Recommended reading order:*

+ *Part 2.0 (Program Flow Diagram)* through *Part 2.3 (Certification Status Framework)*. The architecture of the program and the meaning of the certification mark at each status level.
+ *Part 2.6 (Decision Rules)* and *Part 4 (Lot Testing Schedule)*. The analytical and operational rigor that backs the mark.
+ *Part 2.9 (Supplier Intelligence Sharing)*. The cross-brand collective intelligence system that detects supply-chain problems before they reach finished products.
+ *Part 2.10 (Standards Ratchet Mechanism)*. The mechanism that tightens limits over time as the certified market improves, which is what makes HMTc a forward-moving signal rather than a static gate.
+ *Part 5.5 (Recognition Framework)*. How HMTc compares to USDA Organic, Non-GMO Project, NSF/ANSI 173, and other adjacent programs you may already recognize.



== For Regulators and Public Health Officials


You are reading this manual to assess whether HMTc represents legitimate industry self-regulation that complements federal action levels and EU maximum levels, or whether it is a marketing program dressed as a standard. You need to confirm that the methodology is traceable to documented inputs and that the program drives measurable reduction over time.


*Recommended reading order:*

+ *Part 1.5 (How HMTc Knows What It Knows)*. The evidence base lives at heavymetalindex.com, a public curated corpus of the open literature, architecturally separate from the certification program. Every limit in this manual traces to specific source pages on that wiki.
+ *Part 2.1 (Purpose and Core Principles)*, particularly the framing of action levels as risk-management tools and not safety thresholds.
+ *Part 2.2 (Scope and Analyte Tiering)*. The Tier 1 / Tier 2 metal classification with toxicological rationale for each metal. Includes the aggregate-exposure rationale showing why limits below regulatory action levels are warranted even when a single product complies with federal guidance, because consumers eat across many products and exposures sum.
+ *Part 2.10 (Standards Ratchet Mechanism)*. The data-driven mechanism that commits the program to tighten limits as industry capability improves. Trigger conditions, step-size cap, transition rules, and forward-forecast obligation are all specified.
+ *Part 5.1 (How HMTc Standards Are Set)* and *Part 5.4 (Consolidated Sources Index)*. The methodology described in principle, with the full source attribution.



== For Adversarial Readers


You are reading this manual to find the gaps. You are looking for methodology underspecification, missing toxicological anchors, weak chain-of-custody language, ratchet gaming opportunities, conflict-of-interest framings, or claims that overreach what the literature supports. You will brief your conclusions to a court, a state attorney general's office, or a competing program's leadership.


*Recommended reading order:*

+ *Part 5.2 (Program-Level Adversarial Read)*. Start here. This chapter enumerates the categories of attack the program anticipates, locates each in the manual, and answers them on the merits. Reading this first will save you time identifying which attacks have already been responded to and which (if any) you can advance further.
+ *Part 1.5 (How HMTc Knows What It Knows)*. The evidence base claim. Verify the heavymetalindex.com corpus, the architectural separation from HMTc, and the source-page traceability for limits.
+ *Part 2.10 (Standards Ratchet Mechanism)*. Check whether the trigger conditions, step cap, and transition rules can be gamed.
+ *Each product chapter in Part 3* for the per-product adversarial reads. The product-level attacks are answered chapter by chapter; the program-level attacks live in Part 5.2.
+ *Part 4 (Lot Testing Schedule)*. Look for chain-of-custody, lab-shopping prohibition, and data-integrity language. The program's discipline is operationalized here.



