When speciation is performed, the speciated result (e.g., inorganic arsenic rather than total arsenic) becomes the compliance result for that metal, superseding the total element concentration. Failure to perform required speciation renders the lot ineligible for certification. The reflex speciation trigger of "approaches the limit" is operationally defined as reaching 50% of the applicable HMTc limit for total metal, consistent with the speciation triggers defined in the HMTc Seafood Standards. The Program Operator may lower this threshold further based on risk analysis but may not raise it above 50%.



